<B>4.  PRINCIPLES OF CARTOGRAPHIC COMMUNICATION</B><P><B>
</B><B>Kenneth E. Foote</B>.  Mapping the past:  A survey of microcomputer cartography.  
<I>Historical Methods</I> 25 (1992):  121-131.<P>
<B>5.  POTENTIAL APPLICATIONS OF GIS IN ARCHAEOLOGY</B><P>
<B>David L. Clarke</B>.  Spatial information in archaeology.  <I>Spacial Archaeology</I>, ed. D.L. 
Clarke, 1-32.  New York:  Academic Press, 1977.<P>
<B>Jay K. Johnson, Thomas L. Sever, Scott L.H. Madry, and Harry T. Hoff</B>.  Remote 
sensing and GIS analysis in large scale survey design in north Mississippi.  <I>Southeastern 
Archaeology</I> 7 (1988):  124-131.<P>
<B>Kenneth L. Kvamme</B>.  Terrain form analysis of archaeological location through geographic 
